accordian -- Accordian Solitaire================================    accordianA deck of cards is dealt in a row.  A stack of cards can move one or threeplaces to the left, onto another stack whose top card is the same suit orrank -- closing the gap.  The goal is to squeeze the whole deck into asingle pile.  The book this came from reported that after it publishedthat the game was basically impossible to win, about half a dozen readerswrote in to say they had won it a handful of times in twenty-five years.Keys    d   deal a single card from the deck    D   deal the rest of the deck    f   find the first card that can still move    s   save the layout;  r   restore it;  u   undo the last move    x   exit;  control-R  redraw;  ?  on-screen helpPublic domain -- Eric Lechner, comp.sources.games volume 15, November 1992.Originals in SRC/accordian/ORIG.  Wins are logged to `accordian.wins' inthe directory you play from.